Hi,

I am reporting missing thermal profile and fan control support for the *HP
Omen Transcend 14* (2024/2025).

*System Details:*

   -

   *Board ID:* 8C58
   -

   *Bios Version: *F.12
   -

   *CPU:* Intel Core Ultra 7 155H
   -

   *OS:* Fedora 43 (Kernel 6.13)

*The Issue:* The *hp-wmi* driver loads, but
*/sys/firmware/acpi/platform_profile* is missing. The *hp-wmi-sensors*
driver shows fan RPM, but *pwm1_enable* is stuck in mode 2 (Auto) and
cannot be overridden. Manual EC writes to register 0x66 work but are
immediately reset by the BIOS.

*ACPI Dump (Termbin): **AcpiDump* <https://termbin.com/v4he>  (
https://termbin.com/v4he )

*My Original Post About it: GitHub
<https://github.com/kangtastic/hp-wmi-sensors/issues/5#issue-4040160442> * (
 https://github.com/kangtastic/hp-wmi-sensors/issues/5#issue-4040160442 )

I am happy to test any patches or provide more debug info for this specific
board revision.

Best regards, Uzi


*PS here's the dsl file I got from the acpidump in case you guys need it.*

